{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01124UQmS4PHwx1s9apnY1Pe","type":"tool_result","content":"b0250473 WI-881: Checkpoint 2: SR-238, LLR-026 and TC-026 reconciled after rounds 4 and 5; narrow review 008 filed\neb81debd WI-881: A failure to end the session's tree raises TreeNotEnded, which no ordinary handler can swallow\nb31c3d2a WI-881: The launch owns the child until it hands it over, so an interruption at launch ends it\n0960348f telemetry: session WI-881 verdict accepted\nf2a5fceb telemetry: session 262a252dbb8f4bb9b87380a148a12d2f ADJUDICATE COMPLETED\n04eaa891 WI-881: Re-attest TC-026 under amendment verdict 005\n34da1c74 WI-881: Adjudicate amendment 005: TC-026 is MEANING, blessed\nfa30eece WI-881: Answer sitting 004's return: TC-026's Expected again states SR-026's outcome\n59d417cd telemetry: session WI-881 verdict accepted\ne547d6a2 telemetry: session c59689a1801c4d798e3e124c3cb491a1 ADJUDICATE COMPLETED\n?? docs/reviews/wi-881/009-ADJUDICATE-b025047.md\n?? docs/reviews/wi-881/009-ADJUDICATE-b025047.md.requested\n[decision.D-006]\ndecided = \"Answering full-lane gate 006's F1, the spawn boundary owns the child (and its job) until it returns it, and one try/finally in run_session owns it from there, ending the tree on any exit but a natural one; the waiter's own interrupt handler is retired into that owner. Not built: an interruption that lands inside the standard library's process creation, before the child object reaches the kit's code (POSIX: during Popen's exec handshake, a running child is lost; Windows: at Popen's return, the child is left suspended and never runs). It is recorded as a residual in SR-238's Rationale.\"\nalternative = \"Defer SIGINT around the launch (signal.pthread_sigmask on POSIX, a deferred handler on Windows), which works on the main thread only and adds signal plumbing to every launch.\"\nreversal_cost = \"Low: a later row can add the deferral inside _spawn_session.\"\nwhy_not_escalated = \"The window is the stdlib's own, a few instructions wide, and on Windows the left-behind child never runs; recording it keeps SR-238 true without a main-thread-only mechanism.\"\nreview = \"\"\n\n[decision.D-007]\ndecided = \"Answering narrow review 007's F1, a failure to end the session's tree raises agent_session.TreeNotEnded, a BaseException no `except OSError` or `except Exception` catches, so run_session's launch-error conversion can no longer turn it into a session result. When the cleanup fails while an interrupt is in flight, TreeNotEnded wins (it names what the operator must act on) and the interrupt stays in its chain. One sibling site outside this row's surface is left for its own row: session_service.KeepWarm._ping swallows every exception on its background thread, so a keep-warm session whose tree could not be ended is recorded and dropped. Filed as a follow-up row on trunk at this session's close.\"\nalternative = \"Subclass OSError and audit every handler, or widen this lane into session_service to carry the error from the keep-warm thread to the dispatcher.\"\nreversal_cost = \"Low: one exception class; callers that need cleanup catch BaseException and re-raise, as RESYNC_PACK tells adopters.\"\nwhy_not_escalated = \"It makes the failure unrepresentable as a result at its one owner; the keep-warm site follows the stop-and-file rule for work outside the spec's surface.\"\nreview = \"\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a511e73-e906-4589-9f31-ae73f8534ed7","uuid":"752cd4de-097f-4deb-a8da-e9b1b67c0301","timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:26:22.561Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"b0250473 WI-881: Checkpoint 2: SR-238, LLR-026 and TC-026 reconciled after rounds 4 and 5; narrow review 008 filed\neb81debd WI-881: A failure to end the session's tree raises TreeNotEnded, which no ordinary handler can swallow\nb31c3d2a WI-881: The launch owns the child until it hands it over, so an interruption at launch ends it\n0960348f telemetry: session WI-8